Guard AlifoldZ against a zero-variance shuffle set.

alifoldz.pl divides the native MFE's distance from the shuffle mean by the
shuffle standard deviation. On a candidate whose shuffles all fold to the same
energy that deviation is zero, and the script dies with "Illegal division by
zero" -- a Perl error on stderr, an empty result, and a workflow job that fails
with nothing to explain it.

With this guard it reports the condition and exits non-zero instead. The
workflow already treats a non-result as `NA` (see extract-alifoldz), so the
candidate is recorded as unscored rather than aborting the run or, worse,
being given a plausible-looking number.

Applies to alifoldz.pl from the RNAz sources:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ViennaRNA/RNAz/master/perl/alifoldz.pl

--- alifoldz.pl.orig
+++ alifoldz.pl
@@ -769,9 +769,17 @@
 		}
 	  }
 		
-	  $mean=calc_mean(\@samples);
-	  $stdv=calc_stdv(\@samples);
-	  $z=($native-$mean)/$stdv;
+	  eval {
+	  	$mean=calc_mean(\@samples);
+	  	$stdv=calc_stdv(\@samples);
+		die "Division by zero: mean=$mean, stdv=$stdv" if $stdv == 0;
+	  	$z=($native-$mean)/$stdv;
+	  };
+	  if ($@) {
+		print "**Error: $@";
+		print "0.0\n";
+		die;
+		}
 
 	  $mean=sprintf("%.2f",$mean);
 	  $stdv=sprintf("%.2f",$stdv);
